    1. Choose mode (A or B) randomly, with mode A more common (~75%)
    2. Pick arm_pos randomly from the 8 neighbors of (1,1)
    3. Compute grey_pos and teal_pos using the +3/-3 rotation rule
    4. Build an 11x11 orange grid with pink separator rows/cols at positions 3 and 7
    5. Place red diamond in center cell (1,1) and at arm_pos
    6. If mode B, also place grey diamond at grey_pos and teal at teal_pos
    7. Verify all 4 positions (or 2 for mode A) are distinct (guaranteed by geometry)
